# AGENTS.md

{{name}}: a React single page app (SPA). `npm run build` turns it into static files (`index.html` plus JS and CSS in
`dist/`) that a separate backend serves. There is no server code in this repository, the backend API is reached under
`/api`.

Stack: Vite, React, TypeScript, TanStack Router (file based routing), TanStack Query (server data), Zustand (client
state), Tailwind CSS v4, Vitest with Testing Library, Biome.

## Commands

```bash
npm install
npm run dev          # dev server on http://localhost:5173 with hot reload
npm run build        # type check (tsc) and production build into dist/
npm test             # all unit and component tests once
npm run test:watch   # tests in watch mode
npm run typecheck    # tsc only
npm run check        # biome format + lint with fixes, then tsc
```

Before you finish a change, `npm run check` and `npm test` must pass.

## Where things are

```
src/
  main.tsx              entry point, mounts the providers and the router
  router.tsx            creates the router from routeTree.gen.ts
  routes/               pages, one file per URL (file based routing)
  routeTree.gen.ts      GENERATED from src/routes, never edit it
  features/<feature>/   one vertical slice per topic, see below
  components/ui/        shared, generic building blocks (Button, Card), no feature logic
  components/layout/    the app frame: header, navigation, footer, 404
  lib/                  shared infrastructure: api-client.ts (fetch wrapper), query-client.ts
  stores/               global client state used by many features (theme)
  assets/images|fonts/  images and fonts imported by code or CSS
  styles/app.css        Tailwind entry, design tokens in @theme
  test/                 test setup and render helpers
  config.ts             constants that are the same in every environment
public/                 files served as they are under a fixed URL (favicon, robots.txt)
```

## Features (vertical slices)

Everything that belongs to one topic lives in `src/features/<feature>/`, so a feature can be understood, changed and
deleted in one place:

```
features/<feature>/
  api/          queryOptions, useQuery/useMutation hooks and the request functions (via lib/api-client)
  components/   components of this feature, with their *.spec.tsx next to them
  stores/       Zustand stores only this feature uses
  types.ts      types of this feature (optional)
```

- Only create the subfolders a feature needs.
- A feature may import from `components/`, `lib/`, `stores/` and `config.ts`, but not from another feature. If two
  features need the same code, move it to `components/` or `lib/`.
- Routes stay thin: a file in `src/routes` reads params, loads data in its `loader` and renders feature components.

## How to add things

- **Page:** add a file in `src/routes`, e.g. `src/routes/orders/$orderId.tsx` for `/orders/:orderId`, export
  `Route = createFileRoute('/orders/$orderId')(...)`. Run `npm run dev` or `npm run build` once to regenerate
  `routeTree.gen.ts`. Files starting with `-` in `src/routes` are not routes.
- **API call:** add `features/<feature>/api/<name>.ts` with `queryOptions` and a hook, using `api.get/post/...` from
  `@/lib/api-client`. Paths are relative to `/api`. See `features/health/api/get-health.ts`.
- **Server data** always goes through TanStack Query, never into a Zustand store.
- **Client state** (UI state, drafts): a Zustand store in the feature, or in `src/stores` if it is global.
- **Shared component:** `src/components/ui`, styled with Tailwind classes, no data fetching.
- **Styling:** Tailwind utility classes in the markup; new colors or fonts as tokens in `@theme` in `styles/app.css`.

## Conventions

- Imports use the `@/` alias for `src/`.
- File names are kebab-case (`health-status.tsx`), components PascalCase (`HealthStatus`).
- Tests are `*.spec.ts(x)` next to the code. Use `renderWithProviders` and `renderRoute` from `src/test/render.tsx`,
  stub `fetch` instead of calling a backend, find elements by role or text.
- Environment settings are in `.env.example` (copy to `.env.local`). Only `VITE_*` variables reach the browser.
